    {
      "text": "The combined phrase thus conveys a pivotal, mechanism-driven inversion of pre-modern economies reliant on human and animal power",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "combined"
    },
    {
      "text": "This stability contrasted with continental Europe , where absolutist monarchies often undermined long-term capital accumulation through inconsistent policies",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "stability"
    },
    {
      "text": "Empirical analysis indicates patents facilitated knowledge diffusion without stifling competition, as courts upheld rights selectively, promoting incremental innovation over secrecy",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "analysis"
    },
    {
      "text": "These efficiencies lowered food prices, curbed subsistence crises, and generated capital surpluses from higher yields, fostering a domestic market for industrial goods",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "efficiencies"
    },
    {
      "text": "This financial base, coupled with secure property rights and banking developments, facilitated funding for ventures like canal construction and machinery patents",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "base"
    },
    {
      "text": "This empirical tradition contrasted with continental rationalism , fostering a culture where tinkering and measurement drove progress rather than deduction alone",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "tradition"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pursuit of more reliable power coincided with Britain's abundant coal reserves, which fueled both domestic heating and emerging steam technologies",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "pursuit"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deeper coal mines, necessitated by depleting shallow seams, faced severe flooding, prompting the development of pumping solutions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "mines"
    },
    {
      "text": "James Watt's refinements transformed steam power's viability for broader industry",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "s"
    },
    {
      "text": "This shift underpinned surging productivity, as steam's portability and reliability supported larger-scale operations in metallurgy and manufacturing",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "shift"
    },
    {
      "text": "This hand-operated machine multiplied labor productivity in spinning by allowing coarse yarn production at scale, though it produced weaker thread unsuitable for warp",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "hand"
    },
    {
      "text": "The process, though labor-intensive, eliminated charcoal dependency, allowing iron supply to meet demands for steam engines, bridges, and rails",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "process"
    },
    {
      "text": "By 1836, these trusts had enhanced over 22,000 miles of roadway, enabling faster wagon transport and supporting increased trade",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "trusts"
    },
    {
      "text": "These figures revise earlier optimistic assessments downward, emphasizing that macro-level productivity advances lagged behind sectoral breakthroughs until the 19th century",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "these"
    },
    {
      "text": "This contrasted with mercantilist restrictions, as growing tolerance for bourgeois activities\u2014such as commerce and innovation \u2014encouraged risk-taking and capital accumulation from the mid-18th century onward",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "this"
    },
    {
      "text": "However, financing constraints persisted, with partnerships dominating early industry due to legal barriers on limited liability, limiting scale until mid-19th-century reforms",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "however"
    },
    {
      "text": "This surge resulted from a combination of declining mortality rates preceding and coinciding with industrialization, alongside sustained high fertility",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "surge"
    },
    {
      "text": "Urbanization intensified alongside this demographic shift, transforming Britain into the world's first predominantly urban society",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "urbanization"
    },
    {
      "text": "Urban environments initially exacerbated mortality pressures, countering some national gains in life expectancy",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "initially"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rural-born individuals showed similar trends, implying broader nutritional shortfalls rather than solely urban disamenities",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "rural"
    },
    {
      "text": "Consumption patterns offer mixed signals, with expanded access to certain goods indicating welfare gains for some households",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "offer"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mortality metrics underscore health challenges, particularly in industrializing regions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "particularly"
    },
    {
      "text": "These externalities, while enabling productivity gains, imposed uninternalized costs, including reduced agricultural yields near urban cores from atmospheric deposition",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "while"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unlike Britain , where coal and urban density drove early industrialization, the U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "unlike"
    },
    {
      "text": "Overall, North American adoption emphasized resource endowments\u2014abundant timber, iron, and waterways\u2014over Britain's coal-centric model, fostering decentralized growth that by 1860 positioned the U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "overall"
    },
    {
      "text": "In contrast, non-Western regions experienced delayed or truncated adoption, often undermined by European imperialism and internal institutional rigidities",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "regions"
    },
    {
      "text": "The era's endpoint aligned with World War I's disruptions, though its momentum carried into the interwar period via electrification and petroleum",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "era"
    },
    {
      "text": "This method produced up to 25 tons of steel in 25 minutes, fundamentally shifting economies reliant on wrought iron to steel-based infrastructure",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "method"
    },
    {
      "text": "These innovations spurred electrification of industries, with dynamos powering motors and lights, decoupling energy from steam's locational constraints and boosting productivity through reliable, flexible power",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "innovations"
    },
    {
      "text": "This cycle, now termed the Otto cycle , achieved higher thermal efficiency than prior designs, influencing subsequent engine developments",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "now"
    },
    {
      "text": "This process addressed nitrogen fixation bottlenecks, supporting population growth and averting famines through artificial fertilizer s derived from atmospheric air",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "process"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rockefeller's Standard Oil , which controlled 90% of U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "oil"
    },
    {
      "text": "This shift birthed a more stratified class structure: a burgeoning managerial middle class of engineers and clerks, numbering millions in the U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Industrial_Revolution",
      "agent": "shift"
    },
    {
      "text": "Propositions serve as the foundational elements in logical reasoning , where their truth values enable the construction of arguments by evaluating premises and conclusions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Logic",
