    },
    {
      "text": "Unlike propositional logic, which treats propositions as atomic, first-order logic introduces object-level structure to model mathematical and philosophical arguments more precisely",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Logic",
      "agent": "unlike"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unlike propositional logic, which treats propositions as atomic, first-order logic introduces object-level structure to model mathematical and philosophical arguments more precisely",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Logic",
      "agent": "unlike"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unlike propositional logic, which treats propositions as atomic, first-order logic introduces object-level structure to model mathematical and philosophical arguments more precisely",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Logic",
      "agent": "unlike"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unlike propositional logic, which treats propositions as atomic, first-order logic introduces object-level structure to model mathematical and philosophical arguments more precisely",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Logic",
      "agent": "unlike"
    },
    {
