    },
    {
      "text": "He employed Thomas Edison's phonograph for dictation and note-taking, leveraging the technology to organize complex timelines and character dialogues amid his schedule",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Dracula",
      "agent": "he"
    },
    {
      "text": "He employed Thomas Edison's phonograph for dictation and note-taking, leveraging the technology to organize complex timelines and character dialogues amid his schedule",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Dracula",
      "agent": "he"
    },
    {
      "text": "These revisions, evidenced in auctioned manuscripts from 1913, underscore iterative tightening for narrative economy and impact",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Dracula",
      "agent": "revisions"
    },
    {
      "text": "These revisions, evidenced in auctioned manuscripts from 1913, underscore iterative tightening for narrative economy and impact",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Dracula",
