      "text": "Roman ethics synthesized Greek ideas, with Cicero (106\u201343 BC) adapting Stoic natural law for republican virtue and Seneca emphasizing Stoic endurance under empire",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Ethics",
      "agent": "ethics"
    },
    {
      "text": "These traditions prioritized character formation over consequentialist calculation, influencing later Western moral philosophy by linking ethics to human nature's teleological ends",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Ethics",
      "agent": "traditions"
    },
    {
      "text": "These traditions prioritized character formation over consequentialist calculation, influencing later Western moral philosophy by linking ethics to human nature's teleological ends",
