    },
    {
      "text": "Completeness guarantees that every semantically valid formula (true in all models) is provable syntactically, linking proof-theoretic and model-theoretic notions of truth",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Logic",
      "agent": "formula"
    },
    {
      "text": "Completeness guarantees that every semantically valid formula (true in all models) is provable syntactically, linking proof-theoretic and model-theoretic notions of truth",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Logic",
      "agent": "formula"
    },
    {
