      "source": "Grokipedia-Logic",
      "agent": "s"
    },
    {
      "text": "Logic programming paradigms, exemplified by Prolog , treat programs as sets of logical rules and facts, executing queries via declarative specifications rather than imperative instructions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Logic",
      "agent": "logic"
    },
    {
