    {
      "text": "For instance, a space remains path-connected under homotopy equivalence, linking to the basic property of connectedness",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Topology",
      "agent": "path"
    },
    {
      "text": "The cup product, introduced in Eilenberg and Steenrod's axiomatic treatment, enables computations of products of invariants, such as detecting orientations or torsion",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Topology",
      "agent": "cup"
    },
    {
      "text": "The cup product, introduced in Eilenberg and Steenrod's axiomatic treatment, enables computations of products of invariants, such as detecting orientations or torsion",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Topology",
      "agent": "cup"
    },
    {
      "text": "It focuses on differentiable structures, where manifolds are equipped with atlases of charts allowing smooth transitions, enabling the application of calculus to topological questions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Topology",
      "agent": "it"
