    },
    {
      "text": "Geological remediation techniques address contaminated sites through soil stabilization, where additives like cement or lime bind pollutants to reduce mobility and leachability",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Geology",
      "agent": "geological"
    },
    {
      "text": "By examining rocks, deformations, sediments, volcanic activities, and subsurface waters, these subfields contribute to a holistic understanding of Earth's evolution",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Geology",
      "agent": "examining"
    },
    {
      "text": "Inertial frames are thus equivalent for describing the universe, eliminating any privileged \"rest\" frame and underscoring the relativity of motion in uniform translation",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Theory_of_relativity",
      "agent": "equivalent"
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1971, the Hafele\u2013Keating experiment flew cesium atomic clocks eastward and westward around the Earth on commercial airliners to verify kinematic time dilation",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Theory_of_relativity",
      "agent": "1971"
    },
    {
      "text": "Supporting neurons are glial cells, which are present in the human brain at a ratio of approximately 1:1 to neurons, though this varies by region",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neuroscience",
      "agent": "supporting"
    },
    {
      "text": "Symptomatic treatments target core manifestations of these disorders to improve quality of life and reduce symptom severity",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neuroscience",
      "agent": "symptomatic"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kinase inhibitors targeting tau phosphorylation , like those inhibiting glycogen synthase kinase-3 (GSK-3), have emerged as promising candidates by reducing tau aggregation in preclinical models",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neuroscience",
      "agent": "inhibitors"
    },
    {
      "text": "In rodent studies, neural dust motes have achieved single-neuron resolution recordings with power consumption under 1 \u03bcW, facilitating chronic implantation without foreign body reactions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neuroscience",
      "agent": "rodent"
    },
    {
      "text": "AI adoption in biopharma is increasing, fueling needs for computational neuroscientists who analyze large datasets from fMRI or EEG to accelerate diagnostics and personalized therapies",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neuroscience",
      "agent": "ai"
    },
    {
