    },
    {
      "text": "Meiosis I, the reductional division, begins with prophase I, where homologous chromosomes pair ( synapsis ) via the synaptonemal complex , facilitating crossing over",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Genetics",
      "agent": "chromosomes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Duplications increase gene copy number, potentially causing overexpression; for example, PMP22 duplication results in Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 1A due to excess myelin protein",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Genetics",
      "agent": "potentially"
    },
    {
      "text": "In human females, meiosis features an average of 38 crossovers per cell, compared to 24 in males, with hotspots concentrated in specific genomic regions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Genetics",
      "agent": "meiosis"
    },
    {
      "text": "Epigenetics encompasses heritable changes in gene expression without alterations to the DNA sequence, primarily through DNA methylation , histone modifications , and non-coding RNAs",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Genetics",
      "agent": "epigenetics"
    },
    {
      "text": "As of 2025, developments emphasize in vivo delivery and multiplex editing",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Genetics",
      "agent": "developments"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fact-checked by Grok 4 weeks ago Statistics Statistics is the science of learning from data , and of measuring, controlling, and communicating uncertainty",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Statistics",
      "agent": "fact"
    },
    {
      "text": "Descriptive statistics involves summarizing and describing the features of a dataset , while inferential statistics draws conclusions about a larger population based on a sample",
