    },
    {
      "text": "Mobile expansion intertwined with Web 2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "expansion"
    },
    {
      "text": "0, transforming access from desktop-centric to ubiquitous",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "0"
    },
    {
      "text": "0, transforming access from desktop-centric to ubiquitous",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "0"
    },
    {
      "text": "0, transforming access from desktop-centric to ubiquitous",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "0"
    },
    {
      "text": "0, transforming access from desktop-centric to ubiquitous",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "0"
    },
    {
      "text": "0, transforming access from desktop-centric to ubiquitous",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "0"
    },
    {
      "text": "0, transforming access from desktop-centric to ubiquitous",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "0"
    },
    {
      "text": "By the early 2010s, mobile traffic overtook desktop in some regions, as devices like these reduced barriers to entry compared to fixed broadband",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "like"
    },
    {
      "text": "These developments drove explosive user growth",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "these"
    },
    {
      "text": "Social platforms amplified retention, as users spent increasing time online\u2014averaging 2-3 hours daily by late 2000s\u2014creating feedback loops of engagement and content proliferation",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "platforms"
    },
    {
      "text": "This era's innovations laid groundwork for the internet's mass adoption, though they also introduced challenges like data privacy concerns and echo chambers from algorithmic curation",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "adoption"
    },
    {
      "text": "Efforts like subsidized device programs and undersea cable expansions have narrowed the divide, but sustained infrastructure investment is required to approach universal access",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "like"
    },
    {
      "text": "Individual fiber strands support speeds up to 800 Gbps , far exceeding copper alternatives due to lower attenuation and immunity to electromagnetic interference",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "support"
    },
    {
      "text": "Terrestrial fiber networks extend this backbone inland, with dense deployments in urban areas supporting high-capacity aggregation points",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "deployments"
    },
    {
      "text": "Satellite systems, including low-Earth orbit constellations, offer broadband to remote regions with latencies around 20-50 ms, though capacities remain lower than terrestrial options",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "systems"
    },
    {
      "text": "Global data center capacity exceeded 8 zettabytes of connected storage by 2023 , underscoring their role in hosting Internet services",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "capacity"
    },
    {
      "text": "As of October 2025, regional Internet registries have delegated 119,522 unique AS numbers worldwide",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "2025"
    },
    {
      "text": "As of October 2025, 1,012 IXPs operate globally, facilitating over 80% of peering traffic in major hubs like Frankfurt's DE-CIX and Amsterdam's AMS-IX",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "operate"
    },
    {
      "text": "Redundancy is achieved through multiple disjoint paths, though vulnerabilities persist from cable cuts\u2014averaging 100-150 annually, often repaired within days\u2014and geopolitical risks to landing stations",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "redundancy"
    },
    {
      "text": "Emerging satellite constellations, such as Starlink, supplement but do not displace fiber backbones, handling less than 1% of core intercontinental capacity as of 2025",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "emerging"
    },
    {
