    },
    {
      "text": "PRISM , operational since at least 2007, facilitated bulk collection justified for national security but criticized for lacking targeted warrants and enabling overreach",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "2007"
    },
    {
      "text": "Google , in particular, dominates with trackers embedded in 86% of top websites, enabling comprehensive monitoring of browsing habits",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "google"
    },
    {
      "text": "Resistance to these practices encompasses technical countermeasures, legal advocacy, and policy reforms",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "practices"
    },
    {
      "text": "Efforts to reform or sunset such authorities persist, balancing security claims against empirical evidence of privacy erosions and minimal terrorism prevention gains relative to scale",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "efforts"
    },
    {
      "text": "Outages, Latency, and Resilience Internet outages occur when network infrastructure fails to transmit data , disrupting connectivity for users and services globally",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "network"
    },
    {
      "text": "Common causes include physical damage to undersea cables, software configuration errors, power failures, and deliberate attacks such as DDoS or ransomware",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "common"
    },
    {
      "text": "Economic impacts are severe; a single major outage can cost billions, with countries like the U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "economic"
    },
    {
      "text": "Economic impacts are severe; a single major outage can cost billions, with countries like the U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Internet",
      "agent": "economic"
