      "agent": "further"
    },
    {
      "text": "Army's ongoing evaluations, including prototypes from 2024, focus on integration with infantry gear to enhance endurance without compromising mobility",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "s"
    },
    {
      "text": "Emerging applications include multi-domain robotic collaborations, such as AUKUS trials in 2024 testing UGVs alongside UAVs for joint ISR and logistics in contested environments",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "applications"
    },
    {
      "text": "Logistics robotics primarily involves autonomous mobile robots (AMRs) for warehouse fulfillment and supply chain automation, enhancing speed and scalability amid e-commerce growth",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "chain"
    },
    {
      "text": "Exploration robotics extends to extraterrestrial and oceanic environments, where autonomy is critical due to communication delays and harsh conditions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "exploration"
    },
    {
      "text": "China's Tianwen-2 mission, launched May 29, 2025, employs robotic arms for asteroid sampling and return, marking the nation's first such deep-space endeavor",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "china"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Orpheus AUV, introduced for full-ocean-depth missions, supports prolonged surveys of hydrothermal vents and biodiversity hotspots",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "orpheus"
    },
    {
      "text": "Global sales of professional service robots reached nearly 200,000 units in 2024, reflecting a 9% year-over-year increase amid rising demand for automation in labor-short sectors",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "sales"
    },
    {
      "text": "Delivery robots, such as those from Starship Technologies deployed on U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "technologies"
    },
