      "agent": "technology"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Information Technology and Innovation Foundation (ITIF) has recommended U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "technology"
    },
    {
      "text": "Proponents, including industry leaders, advocate for outcome-based standards over prescriptive ones, enabling faster iteration while maintaining accountability through post-market surveillance",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "proponents"
    },
    {
      "text": "Similarly, initiatives in China aim to establish a full-stack humanoid ecosystem by 2025, emphasizing industrial applications amid global competition",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "similarly"
    },
    {
      "text": "Industrial robotics will advance through enhanced collaborative robots (cobots) and autonomous mobile manipulators, supporting higher automation in manufacturing and logistics",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "advance"
    },
    {
      "text": "These developments hinge on verifiable empirical progress in reliability, as rapid AI gains in simulation do not always translate to physical robustness in real-world settings",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "ai"
    },
    {
      "text": "Proposed mitigations like domain randomization and meta-learning improve generalization but demand ongoing validation, limiting deployment to controlled settings rather than ubiquitous, adaptive systems",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "like"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hardware constraints, particularly energy storage , pose fundamental barriers to scaling mobile and humanoid robots for prolonged, untethered operation",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "hardware"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lithium-ion batteries currently afford humanoids only 2-3 hours of runtime before requiring 1-2 hours to recharge, constraining high-utilization applications like warehouse logistics or elder care",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "hours"
    },
    {
      "text": "Economic and deployment hurdles amplify these technical issues, with high upfront costs, customization needs, and safety certifications impeding mass production",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Robotics",
      "agent": "issues"
    },
    {
      "text": "Both parents had attended the University of Oxford , instilling a strong value on education within the family",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "parents"
    },
    {
      "text": "His birth in Oxford occurred during World War II , as his parents sought a safer location away from London amid wartime bombing risks",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "his"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hawking had three younger siblings: sisters Mary (born 1943) and Philippa (born 1947), and an adopted brother, Edward",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "younger"
    },
    {
      "text": "From an early age, Hawking exhibited mechanical curiosity, frequently disassembling clocks and radios to study their mechanisms before reassembling them",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "hawking"
    },
    {
      "text": "Classmates nicknamed him \"Einstein\" in recognition of his precocity, though his childhood unfolded in a conventional family setting amid post-war recovery",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "classmates"
    },
    {
      "text": "He subsequently transferred to Radlett School before entering St Albans School in September 1952, having passed the eleven-plus examination a year ahead of schedule",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "subsequently"
    },
    {
      "text": "Such hobbies, including an affinity for constructing simple machines, underscored a hands-on approach to inquiry that contrasted with his middling classroom performance",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "hobbies"
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite this, he achieved a first-class honours degree in physics upon graduating in 1962",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "despite"
    },
    {
      "text": "This period marked Hawking's shift from observational astronomy interests to theoretical work on singularities and spacetime geometry , laying groundwork for later collaborations",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "period"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sciama's mentorship emphasized rigorous mathematical analysis over speculative models, fostering Hawking's development as a theorist despite initial difficulties adapting to the demands of original research",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "mentorship"
    },
    {
      "text": "Supervised by Dennis Sciama, the 119-page document applied general relativity to cosmological models, focusing on the implications of the universe's observed expansion",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "supervised"
    },
    {
      "text": "It highlighted \"grave difficulties\" posed by expansion to non-evolving models like the steady-state theory, using causality structures and conformal diagrams to analyze spacetime geometry",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "it"
    },
    {
      "text": "This analysis earned him the 1966 Adams Prize and established singularities as robust predictions of general relativity in cosmological contexts",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "analysis"
    },
    {
      "text": "This cosmological application reversed Penrose's future-directed focus on black holes, proving the universe's initial state involved geodesic incompleteness unavoidable without new physics",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "application"
    },
    {
      "text": "As ALS advanced, Hawking's mobility deteriorated, leading to reliance on assistive devices",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "als"
    },
    {
      "text": "Speech impairment progressed gradually until a 1985 pneumonia episode required tracheostomy, rendering verbal communication impossible and prompting adoption of a computer-based speech synthesizer",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "speech"
    },
    {
      "text": "These adaptations enabled Hawking to maintain intellectual productivity and public engagement, authoring books, delivering lectures via the synthesizer , and collaborating internationally",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "adaptations"
    },
    {
      "text": "Care involved round-the-clock nursing and technological upgrades, including software from Intel that optimized communication efficiency",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "care"
    },
    {
      "text": "Larger black holes gain mass from infalling cosmic radiation, but isolation would cause gradual shrinkage, accelerating as mass decreases due to rising temperature",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "mass"
    },
    {
      "text": "Full evaporation implies black holes dissolve completely, releasing their energy quantum mechanically, though the endpoint mechanism\u2014potentially explosive for small remnants\u2014remains unresolved without quantum gravity theory",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "completely"
    },
    {
      "text": "The zeroth law states that the surface gravity \u03ba \\kappa \u03ba is constant over the event horizon for stationary black holes",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "law"
    },
    {
      "text": "The second law is Hawking's area theorem itself: d A \u2265 0 dA \\geq 0 d A \u2265 0",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "second"
    },
    {
      "text": "These laws applied to stationary , axisymmetric black holes described by the no-hair theorem , highlighting causal structure over microscopic details",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "laws"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hawking initially rejected this, contending that quantum effects near the horizon could allow area decrease without entropy gain, violating the second law",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "initially"
    },
    {
      "text": "This framework resolved classical paradoxes by treating horizon area as a macroscopic entropy measure, though its microscopic origin remains tied to quantum gravity unresolved issues",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "framework"
    },
    {
      "text": "The CTC under his leadership published findings challenging certain multiverse interpretations by highlighting observational constraints from cosmic microwave background data",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "ctc"
    },
    {
      "text": "These talks, transcribed on his official estate site, prioritized data from telescopes like Hubble over unverified hypotheses, influencing public understanding of cosmology's empirical foundations",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "talks"
    },
    {
      "text": "His talks, archived and disseminated online, prioritized first-principles derivations\u2014e",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "talks"
    },
    {
      "text": "His talks, archived and disseminated online, prioritized first-principles derivations\u2014e",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "talks"
    },
    {
      "text": "His talks, archived and disseminated online, prioritized first-principles derivations\u2014e",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "talks"
    },
    {
      "text": "His talks, archived and disseminated online, prioritized first-principles derivations\u2014e",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "talks"
    },
    {
      "text": "His talks, archived and disseminated online, prioritized first-principles derivations\u2014e",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "talks"
    },
    {
      "text": ", deriving the universe's finite age from Hubble's constant measurements\u2014over institutional dogmas, fostering causal understanding among audiences",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "deriving"
    },
    {
