    {
      "text": ", deriving the universe's finite age from Hubble's constant measurements\u2014over institutional dogmas, fostering causal understanding among audiences",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "deriving"
    },
    {
      "text": "The couple had three children: son Robert , born in May 1967; daughter Lucy , born in November 1970; and son Timothy, born in 1979",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "couple"
    },
    {
      "text": "The couple separated in 1990 and divorced in 1995, after which Wilde married Jones in 1997",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "couple"
    },
    {
      "text": "The marriage lasted until their divorce in October 2006, amid reports of incompatibility and prior allegations against Mason",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "marriage"
    },
    {
      "text": "Post-tracheostomy, he depended on positive airway pressure devices, initially part-time and later continuously, to maintain breathing as diaphragmatic muscles weakened",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "tracheostomy"
    },
    {
      "text": "By the 2000s , Hawking was fully quadriplegic, with only minimal cheek muscle control remaining for communication interfaces, yet his cognitive functions stayed unimpaired throughout",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "2000s"
    },
    {
      "text": "The wheelchair's battery also powered an integrated computer system, enabling portability for lectures, research, and daily travel",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "wheelchair"
    },
    {
      "text": "A critical advancement occurred in 1985 after emergency tracheotomy due to pneumonia , which eliminated Hawking's natural speech",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "advancement"
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite offers of more advanced synthesizers, Hawking retained his familiar voice for continuity, rejecting changes that altered its distinctive timbre",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "despite"
    },
    {
      "text": "Must try it for my thesis,\" and returned in episodes through 2010, often correcting characters' scientific errors",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "thesis"
    },
    {
      "text": "These roles, spanning over two decades, showcased Hawking's humor and reinforced his image as an accessible scientific authority",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "roles"
    },
    {
      "text": "In live performances and sketches, Hawking extended his media presence to comedy stages",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "hawking"
    },
    {
      "text": "His cameos and writings collectively humanized theoretical physics , drawing public interest to cosmology amid his personal challenges with ALS , without relying on sensationalism",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "collectively"
    },
    {
      "text": "Through these efforts, Hawking promoted awareness of ALS-specific needs while challenging underestimations of disabled individuals' potential",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "efforts"
    },
    {
      "text": "Philosophy has not kept up with modern developments in science, particularly physics",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "philosophy"
    },
    {
      "text": "For instance, debates over quantum interpretations (e",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
