      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "he"
    },
    {
      "text": "He viewed Donald Trump as a \"demagogue\" appealing to base instincts and warned that the 2017 U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "he"
    },
    {
      "text": "He viewed Donald Trump as a \"demagogue\" appealing to base instincts and warned that the 2017 U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "he"
    },
    {
      "text": "These bets highlighted his willingness to stake reputation on theoretical predictions, though he lost most, underscoring the empirical challenges in confirming exotic astrophysical claims",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "bets"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hawking bet that information falling into a black hole is irretrievably lost, while Preskill argued for preservation",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "bet"
    },
    {
      "text": "The couple had three children: Robert , born in May 1967; Lucy , born in November 1970; and Timothy , born in April 1979",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "couple"
    },
    {
      "text": "The marriage ended in divorce in October 2006",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "marriage"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hawking consistently denied abuse , refused to cooperate fully with prosecutors, and no charges were filed against Mason",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "consistently"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hawking maintained professional associations that occasionally intersected with controversial figures, such as attending a 2006 conference on gravity and fundamental physics in St",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "hawking"
    },
    {
      "text": "On ethical matters of end-of-life choices, Hawking initially described euthanasia as \"a great mistake\" in 2006",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "initially"
    },
    {
      "text": "He advocated for laws to restrict such modifications in humans, emphasizing the need to preserve natural evolution amid technological pressures",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "he"
    },
    {
      "text": "Physicist Sean Carroll assessed Hawking's work on gravity as surpassing all post-Einstein contributions in depth and influence",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "carroll"
    },
    {
      "text": "Peter Higgs , in 2018 commentary, implied Hawking's boldness in speculation sometimes prioritized visibility over caution, contrasting with professional norms favoring empirical validation",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "commentary"
    },
    {
      "text": "ResearchGate discussions among physicists in 2022 noted inconsistencies in his cosmological claims, questioning adherence to scientific norms in public discourse",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "among"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prospect Magazine's 2021 review similarly critiqued deification, attributing inflated reputation to narrative appeal over empirical breakthroughs",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "similarly"
    },
    {
      "text": "The death occurred peacefully, as confirmed by statements from his family, who noted he had passed early in the morning surrounded by loved ones",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "death"
    },
    {
      "text": "His body was cremated following the death, with ashes later interred at Westminster Abbey",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "body"
    },
    {
      "text": "Honors, Awards, and Institutions Hawking was appointed Commander of the Order of the British Empire (CBE) in 1982 for his contributions to science",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "institutions"
    },
    {
      "text": "He received the Companion of Honour in the 1989 New Year Honours , recognizing his exceptional service in the advancement of human knowledge",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "he"
    },
    {
      "text": "He held the position of Lucasian Professor of Mathematics at the University of Cambridge from 1979 to 2009, a chair previously occupied by Isaac Newton",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "university"
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier, in 1977, he was appointed Professor of Gravitational Physics at Cambridge",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "he"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hawking was elected a Fellow of the Royal Society (FRS) in 1974",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "hawking"
    },
    {
      "text": "In total, Hawking earned thirteen honorary degrees from universities worldwide",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "hawking"
    },
    {
      "text": "These results provided a causal argument for the Big Bang as a singularity and reinforced predictions of black hole interiors",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "results"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hawking co-authored the 1973 monograph The Large Scale Structure of Space-Time with George F",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "hawking"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ellis , a foundational text in general relativity that rigorously analyzed global spacetime properties, causal structure, and the inevitability of singularities",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "rigorously"
    },
    {
      "text": "This introduced the information paradox, as the process appears to destroy information violating quantum unitarity, a tension unresolved in subsequent theoretical frameworks",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "this"
    },
    {
      "text": "It was updated in an illustrated edition in 1996 to incorporate diagrams and clarify complex ideas",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "it"
    },
    {
      "text": "Subsequent works expanded on these themes with visual aids and collaborations",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "works"
    },
    {
      "text": "My Brief History (2013) offered an autobiographical account of his career and challenges",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "history"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hawking co-authored a series of children's books with his daughter Lucy Hawking to introduce young readers to astrophysics through adventure narratives",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "hawking"
    },
    {
      "text": "A later posthumous work, You and the Universe (2024), adapted Hawking's ideas for children, encouraging inquiry into cosmic questions with illustrations",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "later"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beyond books, Hawking engaged in outreach through public lectures and media productions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "beyond"
    },
    {
      "text": "He delivered synthesized-voice talks on topics like the universe's origins, such as his 2007 Oppenheimer Lecture at UC Berkeley discussing cosmology without divine intervention",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "he"
    },
    {
      "text": "Documentaries included Into the Universe with Stephen Hawking (2010), a three-part series exploring time travel , aliens, and the universe's fate using CGI visualizations",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "documentaries"
    },
    {
      "text": "These efforts reached millions, blending rigorous science with accessible formats to foster public interest in theoretical physics",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Stephen_Hawking",
      "agent": "efforts"
    },
    {
      "text": "He constructed rudimentary inventions, such as a bug-powered propeller and a waterwheel, drawing inspiration from his mother's devices and the local water-powered mills",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "he"
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite the family's Serbian ethnic and Orthodox cultural roots in a multi-ethnic empire, Tesla's childhood emphasized self-reliance and empirical curiosity over rote tradition",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "despite"
    },
    {
      "text": "This marked the end of his structured higher education in Austria-Hungary, after which he sought practical engineering roles",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "this"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tesla's Paris role underscored the practical constraints of contemporary electrical technology, fueling his subsequent critiques of DC's inefficiencies",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "s"
    },
    {
      "text": "The concept required no mechanical switching, promising higher reliability and scalability for industrial applications, though Tesla initially lacked resources to prototype it fully",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "concept"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Budapest epiphany thus marked the origin of the polyphase AC system, patented years later as U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "budapest"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Budapest epiphany thus marked the origin of the polyphase AC system, patented years later as U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "budapest"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Budapest epiphany thus marked the origin of the polyphase AC system, patented years later as U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "budapest"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Budapest epiphany thus marked the origin of the polyphase AC system, patented years later as U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "budapest"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Budapest epiphany thus marked the origin of the polyphase AC system, patented years later as U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "budapest"
    },
    {
      "text": "Patent 381,968 (May 1, 1888), but rooted in Tesla's unaided empirical reasoning rather than incremental adaptation of prior single-phase work",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "1888"
    },
    {
      "text": "The letter stated: \"My dear Edison: I know two great men, and you are one of them",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "letter"
    },
    {
      "text": "In December 1884, Tesla partnered with Robert Lane, an attorney, and Benjamin V",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "tesla"
    },
    {
      "text": "Arnold, a businessman providing capital, to establish the Tesla Electric Light & Manufacturing Company in Rahway, New Jersey",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "businessman"
    },
    {
      "text": "The venture capitalized on Tesla's U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "venture"
    },
    {
      "text": "The venture capitalized on Tesla's U",
