    },
    {
      "text": "The venture capitalized on Tesla's U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "venture"
    },
    {
      "text": "The company constructed a laboratory and manufacturing facility in Rahway, where Tesla oversaw the production of arc lamps and generators",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "company"
    },
    {
      "text": "The episode underscored Tesla's focus on practical commercialization but also investor priorities favoring short-term arc lighting profits over his broader alternating current ambitions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "episode"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shortly thereafter, George Westinghouse, seeking to challenge Thomas Edison's direct current (DC) dominance, licensed Tesla's key AC patents, encompassing the induction motor (U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "westinghouse"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shortly thereafter, George Westinghouse, seeking to challenge Thomas Edison's direct current (DC) dominance, licensed Tesla's key AC patents, encompassing the induction motor (U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "westinghouse"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shortly thereafter, George Westinghouse, seeking to challenge Thomas Edison's direct current (DC) dominance, licensed Tesla's key AC patents, encompassing the induction motor (U",
