    },
    {
      "text": "This milestone, leveraging Tesla's patents for polyphase distribution (including U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "milestone"
    },
    {
      "text": "Patent 390,721 for dynamos), propelled global adoption of AC grids and underscored the War of Currents' resolution in favor of alternating systems",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "patent"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tesla modified existing apparatus, including Ruhmkorff induction coils, to generate potentials up to hundreds of thousands of volts at frequencies exceeding 10,000 cycles per second",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "tesla"
    },
    {
      "text": "This alternator , operational by 1890 , enabled sustained high-frequency output without the limitations of interrupter-based systems",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "this"
    },
    {
      "text": "These wireless lighting experiments highlighted the feasibility of transmitting electrical energy through space or insulating media at high frequencies, bypassing traditional conductors",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "wireless"
    },
    {
      "text": "However, practical challenges, such as energy losses and safety concerns with high voltages, limited immediate commercialization",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "however"
    },
    {
      "text": "He envisioned applications in torpedoes, vehicles, and automata, terming it \"teleautomation,\" though initial skepticism labeled it a hoax until verified by patent examiners",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "he"
    },
    {
      "text": "This predated widespread radio applications and laid groundwork for modern remote control, distinct from Marconi's signaling by incorporating directive control logic",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "this"
    },
    {
      "text": "Experiments commenced around June 15, as documented in Tesla's detailed daily notes, which recorded observations on resonance, ground currents, and atmospheric electricity",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "experiments"
    },
    {
      "text": "Central to the work was the development of a \"magnifying transmitter,\" an advanced resonant transformer Tesla designed to amplify electrical oscillations to extreme voltages",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "central"
    },
    {
      "text": "Local residents noted side effects, such as luminous discharges from the ground and sparks jumping between objects, attributed to the intense electromagnetic fields",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "residents"
    },
    {
      "text": "Construction commenced in June 1901 following a $150,000 investment from J",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "construction"
    },
    {
      "text": "Construction commenced in June 1901 following a $150,000 investment from J",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "construction"
    },
    {
      "text": "Construction commenced in June 1901 following a $150,000 investment from J",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "construction"
    },
    {
      "text": "Construction commenced in June 1901 following a $150,000 investment from J",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "construction"
    },
    {
      "text": "Construction commenced in June 1901 following a $150,000 investment from J",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "construction"
    },
    {
      "text": "Morgan, initially intended to support transatlantic wireless telegraphy akin to Guglielmo Marconi's achievements, leveraging Tesla's prior Colorado Springs research on high-voltage, high-frequency currents",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "initially"
    },
    {
      "text": "Construction stalled despite the tower's near-completion by mid-1903, as Tesla's unsuccessful appeals to other investors, including the Russian tsar, failed to materialize further capital",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "construction"
    },
    {
      "text": "By 1905, the site faced foreclosure proceedings from Warden over back taxes, and Tesla abandoned active work on Wardenclyffe",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "site"
    },
    {
      "text": "The laboratory persisted until its own foreclosure in 1922, marking the definitive end of Tesla's most ambitious terrestrial project",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "laboratory"
    },
    {
      "text": "Patent 514,169 on February 6, 1894, following an application filed August 19, 1893",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "1894"
    },
    {
      "text": "The invention underscored valid principles of mechanical resonance but saw limited adoption, overshadowed by Tesla's electrical pursuits and unverified grander applications like earthquake induction",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "invention"
    },
    {
      "text": "Other Devices and Unfulfilled Projects Tesla proposed the \"teleforce\" beam, a charged-particle weapon intended for defensive purposes, in the late 1930s",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "devices"
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1901, Tesla patented an apparatus for utilizing radiant energy (U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "tesla"
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1901, Tesla patented an apparatus for utilizing radiant energy (U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "tesla"
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1901, Tesla patented an apparatus for utilizing radiant energy (U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "tesla"
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1901, Tesla patented an apparatus for utilizing radiant energy (U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "tesla"
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1901, Tesla patented an apparatus for utilizing radiant energy (U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "tesla"
    },
    {
      "text": "Modern assessments view it as speculative pseudoscience, unfeasible without advanced neuroimaging unavailable in Tesla's era",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "without"
    },
    {
      "text": "These late-career endeavors highlight Tesla's visionary scope but underscore practical barriers, including investor wariness after repeated financial setbacks",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "career"
    },
    {
      "text": "He subsequently developed his alternating current (AC) polyphase system, obtaining key patents in 1888, which George Westinghouse licensed for $60,000 plus royalties",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "subsequently"
    },
    {
      "text": "Edison, defending his DC investments, launched a campaign to portray AC as inherently dangerous, funding demonstrations by engineer Harold P",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "edison"
    },
    {
      "text": "Guglielmo Marconi, beginning experiments in 1894-1895, achieved short-range wireless telegraphy by 1895 but filed his first U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "marconi"
    },
    {
      "text": "Guglielmo Marconi, beginning experiments in 1894-1895, achieved short-range wireless telegraphy by 1895 but filed his first U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "marconi"
    },
    {
      "text": "Guglielmo Marconi, beginning experiments in 1894-1895, achieved short-range wireless telegraphy by 1895 but filed his first U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "marconi"
    },
    {
      "text": "Guglielmo Marconi, beginning experiments in 1894-1895, achieved short-range wireless telegraphy by 1895 but filed his first U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "marconi"
    },
    {
      "text": "Guglielmo Marconi, beginning experiments in 1894-1895, achieved short-range wireless telegraphy by 1895 but filed his first U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "marconi"
    },
    {
      "text": "Over the next three years, Marconi revised his applications multiple times amid appeals, and on June 28, 1904, a different examiner granted U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "marconi"
    },
    {
      "text": "Over the next three years, Marconi revised his applications multiple times amid appeals, and on June 28, 1904, a different examiner granted U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "marconi"
    },
    {
