    },
    {
      "text": "Investments in bioenergy are projected to reach $16 billion in 2025, a 13% increase, driven by policy support despite slower capacity growth in advanced economies",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "investments"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lifecycle greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions from bioenergy vary widely but are not inherently zero or lower than fossil fuels without strict sustainability measures",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "vary"
    },
    {
      "text": "Biofuel production from crops can drive indirect land-use change, including deforestation , increasing emissions by 20-100% compared to gasoline in lifecycle analyses",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "can"
    },
    {
      "text": "High dependence on biomass in developing countries exacerbates deforestation and soil degradation, contributing to 15% of global anthropogenic GHG emissions from land-use changes",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "high"
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite these issues, bioenergy's dispatchable nature provides grid flexibility, though its scalability is limited by feedstock availability and lower energy density compared to fossil fuels",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "despite"
    },
    {
      "text": "Department of Energy (DOE) pilots in the 1970s, such as the Fenton Hill project in New Mexico , which demonstrated feasibility but highlighted stimulation challenges",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "department"
    },
    {
      "text": "EGS holds potential to supply 20% of U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "holds"
    },
    {
      "text": "EGS holds potential to supply 20% of U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "holds"
    },
    {
      "text": "EGS holds potential to supply 20% of U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "holds"
    },
    {
      "text": "EGS holds potential to supply 20% of U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "holds"
    },
    {
      "text": "EGS holds potential to supply 20% of U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "holds"
    },
    {
      "text": "Projections indicate LCOE could reach grid parity by 2027 in favorable sites with capacity factors over 90%, outperforming intermittent renewables in reliability",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "projections"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deployment faces technical hurdles including maintaining fracture permeability over decades, as mineral precipitation and thermal contraction can reduce flow rates by 50% or more post-stimulation",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "deployment"
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite these, empirical data from recent pilots affirm EGS's causal potential for firm, zero-carbon power if economic barriers subside through iterative field testing",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "field"
    },
    {
      "text": "These innovations bypass rare-earth dependencies, though site-specific geography limits widespread adoption compared to electrochemical rivals",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "adoption"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermal energy storage advancements, particularly in molten salt configurations, facilitate dispatchable output from concentrated solar power by storing heat at 565\u00b0C for 10+ hours",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "output"
    },
    {
      "text": "Innovations like single-tank thermocline designs with particulate fillers reduce material use by 30-50% versus two-tank systems, enhancing cost-effectiveness for hybrid renewable plants",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "innovations"
    },
    {
      "text": "Efficiencies exceed 95% for sensible heat retention, though corrosion and freezing risks necessitate alloyed salts or additives",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "efficiencies"
    },
    {
      "text": "However, manufacturing scalability and interface dendrite formation persist as barriers, with commercial grid deployments projected post-2030 despite lab efficiencies nearing 90%",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "however"
    },
    {
      "text": "These technologies collectively aim to lower levelized cost of storage below $100/kWh by 2030, contingent on material innovations and policy support",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "technologies"
    },
    {
      "text": "A 2024 analysis concludes SBSP remains speculative, as ground-based alternatives continue to scale more rapidly and cheaply",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "remains"
    },
    {
      "text": "These concepts, while theoretically superior in resource access, hinge on overcoming engineering and economic obstacles that have delayed prototypes for decades",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "while"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wind power exhibits variability driven by wind speed distributions, with onshore capacity factors averaging 36% fleet-wide in the U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "driven"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wind power exhibits variability driven by wind speed distributions, with onshore capacity factors averaging 36% fleet-wide in the U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
