    {
      "text": "Additionally, collisions with turbines result in significant wildlife mortality; estimates from U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "additionally"
    },
    {
      "text": "A global assessment notes that such developments in biodiversity hotspots exacerbate fragmentation, potentially increasing extinction risks for endemic species",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "potentially"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hydropower installations, while more land-efficient at 5-10 square meters per megawatt-hour, cause profound habitat inundation through reservoir creation, displacing terrestrial and aquatic ecosystems",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "meters"
    },
    {
      "text": "Solar panels demand significant silver (around 20 grams per panel) for conductive paste, alongside copper for wiring and silicon purification processes that involve energy-intensive refining",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "copper"
    },
    {
      "text": "Copper and lithium operations face acute water stress risks, with over 50% of projected supply exposed to scarcity in arid regions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "50"
    },
    {
      "text": "These impacts extend to habitat displacement and behavioral alterations, where operational turbines deter or fragment use of surrounding areas by avian and mammalian species",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "alterations"
    },
    {
      "text": "Solar photovoltaic installations contribute to habitat loss, fragmentation, and degradation, primarily through land clearing that displaces native vegetation and wildlife",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "degradation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Medium-sized solar farms result in proportionally higher losses of seminatural habitats compared to larger facilities, due to greater edge effects and perimeter disturbances",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "medium"
    },
    {
      "text": "While some designs incorporate pollinator-friendly vegetation under panels, empirical evidence indicates these measures often fail to fully offset initial biodiversity declines from site development",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "evidence"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hydroelectric dams disrupt aquatic ecosystems by blocking fish migration routes, leading to population isolation and declines in migratory species",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "ecosystems"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tailrace discharges exacerbate these effects by causing fish injury, mortality, and delayed migrations that impair spawning success",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "effects"
    },
    {
      "text": "Biomass energy production, particularly from woody sources, drives deforestation and biodiversity loss through harvesting that removes standing forest s and disrupts carbon sinks",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "biodiversity"
    },
    {
      "text": "Global demand for wood pellets is forecasted to triple by 2030, accelerating habitat fragmentation in tropical regions and contributing to species declines",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Renewable_energy",
      "agent": "pellets"
    },
    {
