    {
      "text": "These archives reveal recurrent glacial-interglacial cycles during the Pleistocene epoch, with global temperatures fluctuating by approximately 4\u20137\u00b0C between cold glacial maxima and warmer interglacials",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "cycles"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tree-ring \u03b4\u00b9\u2078O from the European Alps reveals a significant drying and cooling trend over the Holocene, aligned with decreasing summer insolation from orbital precession",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "alps"
    },
    {
      "text": "These shifts occurred on timescales of centuries to millennia, with regional temperature anomalies often exceeding 1\u00b0C, demonstrating the Earth's climate system's sensitivity to natural forcings",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "shifts"
    },
    {
      "text": "This warmth appears regionally pronounced rather than globally uniform, with pollen and speleothem records from Europe corroborating milder conditions conducive to viticulture in Britain",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "regionally"
    },
    {
      "text": "While not synchronously global, borehole and documentary evidence from China and South America indicate concurrent warm anomalies in select regions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "while"
    },
    {
      "text": "These events underscore pre-industrial climate dynamism, with recovery toward 1900 aligning with solar rebound and diminished volcanism",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "events"
    },
    {
      "text": "These independent analyses converge on a net warming of approximately 1",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "analyses"
