    {
      "text": "Reconstructions from 945 tide gauges from 1900 to 2022 confirm ongoing rise but highlight regional differences due to vertical land motion and local subsidence",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "reconstructions"
    },
    {
      "text": "Land-based ice contributes significantly to sea level rise through mass loss",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "land"
    },
    {
      "text": "The World Glacier Monitoring Service reports the 2022-2024 period as the largest three-year mass loss on record for monitored glaciers",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "world"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the United States, for example, drought frequency has not trended upward when normalized for natural cycles, challenging narratives of climate-driven aridification",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "united"
    },
    {
      "text": "Peer-reviewed critiques emphasize that disaster cost escalations, such as U",
