      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "ar6"
    },
    {
      "text": "Terrestrial ecosystems show amplified responses in high-latitude and high-elevation regions, where warming exceeds the global average",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "ecosystems"
    },
    {
      "text": "These changes disrupt alpine and Arctic habitats, promoting shrub encroachment over tundra and increasing wildfire risk in boreal forests via drier conditions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "changes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Uncertainties persist in attributing specific biodiversity declines solely to climate, as synergistic drivers like invasive species and overexploitation often dominate empirical datasets",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "persist"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the United States, climate-related events from 1980 to early 2025 inflicted over $2",
