    {
      "text": "Midwest and parts of Europe and Asia, exacerbating food price volatility and contributing to undernutrition in low-income populations",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "asia"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conversely, fewer cold-related deaths in temperate zones partially offset these, though net global health costs are projected positive in most models",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "conversely"
    },
    {
      "text": "In agriculture, CO2 fertilization has demonstrably increased crop yields",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "demonstrably"
    },
    {
      "text": "Experimental evidence confirms that higher CO2 levels improve water-use efficiency in crops, mitigating drought stress and supporting higher productivity under elevated temperatures",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "experimental"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mortality patterns reveal that cold-related deaths substantially outnumber heat-related ones globally",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "cold"
    },
    {
      "text": "A comprehensive analysis found excess cold-attributable deaths at roughly 9 times the rate of heat-related deaths, totaling about 4",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
      "agent": "analysis"
    },
    {
      "text": "A comprehensive analysis found excess cold-attributable deaths at roughly 9 times the rate of heat-related deaths, totaling about 4",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Climate_change",
