    },
    {
      "text": "This decay underscores the neutron's role in stellar nucleosynthesis and underscores the weak interaction's influence on matter stability",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neutron",
      "agent": "decay"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chadwick received the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1935 for this discovery, which fundamentally advanced understanding of nuclear structure",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neutron",
      "agent": "chadwick"
    },
    {
      "text": "In particle physics units, this equates to an energy of 939",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neutron",
