      "source": "Grokipedia-Neutron",
      "agent": "time"
    },
    {
      "text": "Emergency protocols involve decontamination and medical triage based on dose reconstructions, prioritizing anti-emetics and cytokines for doses >1 Gy equivalent",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neutron",
      "agent": "medical"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beam experiments, conversely, measure the lifetime by detecting protons produced from neutron beta decay within a controlled beam , normalizing to the incident neutron flux",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neutron",
      "agent": "conversely"
    },
    {
      "text": "Recent theoretical work suggests quantum effects like differing neutron coherence states or collision-induced decay enhancements could contribute, though no consensus exists",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neutron",
      "agent": "work"
    },
    {
      "text": "These materials address limitations in pulse shape discrimination, enabling better separation of neutron and gamma signals in mixed radiation fields",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neutron",
      "agent": "limitations"
    },
    {
      "text": "Such detectors leverage solid-state advantages, including compactness and radiation hardness, suitable for high-flux environments like spallation sources",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Neutron",
      "agent": "state"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dysregulation of these checkpoints, often via mutations in tumor suppressors like p53, can lead to uncontrolled proliferation characteristic of cancer",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Biology",
      "agent": "often"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fungi constitute a monophyletic kingdom within the Opisthokonta supergroup, sharing a common ancestor with animals but distinguished by absorptive heterotrophy and chitinous cell walls",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Biology",
      "agent": "kingdom"
    },
    {
      "text": "Population regulation refers to the biotic and abiotic mechanisms that stabilize fluctuations around K, preventing indefinite exponential increase or unchecked decline",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Biology",
