    },
    {
      "text": "These distances become more intuitive through light travel times, which reveal the finite speed of information propagation even at light speed",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Solar_System",
      "agent": "distances"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sun light reaches Earth in about 8 minutes and 20 seconds, illuminating daily solar influences on our planet",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Solar_System",
      "agent": "light"
    },
    {
      "text": "This zone is calculated using models that balance incoming stellar radiation with planetary thermal emission, incorporating factors such as atmospheric composition and albedo",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Solar_System",
      "agent": "zone"
    },
    {
      "text": "More advanced models refine these by including greenhouse effects and cloud feedbacks",
