    {
      "text": "0 followed in 1996 via RFC 1945, introducing methods like POST and basic authentication, reflecting lessons from early deployments",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "0"
    },
    {
      "text": "0 followed in 1996 via RFC 1945, introducing methods like POST and basic authentication, reflecting lessons from early deployments",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "0"
    },
    {
      "text": "The development of graphical web browsers accelerated adoption by making the web accessible to non-technical users",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "development"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mosaic browser, released in 1993 by the National Center for Supercomputing Applications , introduced inline images and intuitive navigation, inspiring commercial spin-offs",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "mosaic"
    },
    {
      "text": "This infrastructure shift enabled internet service providers to offer paid dial-up and dedicated connections, lowering barriers for enterprises and consumers",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "shift"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mass adoption followed, fueled by affordable personal computers, expanding dial-up services from providers like AOL , and the dot-com era's influx of e-commerce sites",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "adoption"
    },
    {
      "text": "By late 1993, over 500 web servers existed, representing 1% of total internet traffic \u2014a modest but rapidly expanding share that ballooned with commercial incentives",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "servers"
    },
    {
      "text": "By 2000, global Internet users\u2014predominantly accessing via the Web\u2014reached approximately 413 million, reflecting exponential growth driven by improved browser technologies and dial-up connectivity",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "users"
    },
    {
      "text": "The early 2000s marked the shift to Web 2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "2000s"
    },
    {
      "text": "The early 2000s marked the shift to Web 2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "2000s"
    },
    {
      "text": "The early 2000s marked the shift to Web 2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "2000s"
    },
    {
      "text": "The early 2000s marked the shift to Web 2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "2000s"
    },
    {
      "text": "The early 2000s marked the shift to Web 2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "2000s"
    },
    {
      "text": "0 paradigms, emphasizing user-generated content and interactivity, which dramatically increased engagement and site proliferation",
      "source": "Grokipedia-World_Wide_Web",
      "agent": "paradigms"
