    {
      "text": "5 in optimized designs, contrasting with thermal reactors' consumption-only mode",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "5"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coolant choices like sodium provide high thermal conductivity and boiling points above 800\u00b0C, supporting higher outlet temperatures (500-550\u00b0C) for improved thermodynamic efficiency over water-cooled systems",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "like"
    },
    {
      "text": "They also enable closed fuel cycles, recycling spent fuel to minimize geological repository needs",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "enable"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prominent SMR examples include NuScale Power's VOYGR, a pressurized water reactor with 77 MWe modules using integral steam generators for compactness; the U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "prominent"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prominent SMR examples include NuScale Power's VOYGR, a pressurized water reactor with 77 MWe modules using integral steam generators for compactness; the U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
