    },
    {
      "text": "These innovations promise proliferation resistance and accident tolerance but require validation against empirical data from limited operational hours, contrasting with proven Gen II/III safety records",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "innovations"
    },
    {
      "text": "The realization of a controlled chain reaction followed in the United States under the Manhattan Project",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "realization"
    },
    {
      "text": "Postwar efforts shifted toward civilian applications",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "efforts"
    },
    {
      "text": "These milestones transitioned fission from wartime secrecy to international peaceful energy pursuits, despite early designs prioritizing dual-use capabilities",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "milestones"
    },
    {
      "text": "Concurrently, utilities in Europe and Japan placed orders for similar light-water designs, leveraging technologies proven in naval propulsion programs, which facilitated scalability and regulatory familiarity",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "concurrently"
    },
    {
      "text": "Over 150,000 evacuations followed precautionary measures, contributing to around 2,300 indirect deaths from stress and relocation, exceeding direct nuclear harms",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "evacuations"
    },
    {
      "text": "However, gross capacity additions continued, particularly in Asia , leading to a gradual revival by the early 2020s",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "additions"
    },
    {
      "text": "High capacity factors, averaging 83% globally in 2024, further enhanced output, pushing nuclear electricity generation to a record 2,817 TWh that year, surpassing pre-Fukushima peaks",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "factors"
    },
    {
      "text": "This process occurs in specialized facilities handling alpha radiation , with waste minimized through recycling scrap UO2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "process"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fuel burnup quantifies the energy extracted per unit mass of heavy metal , typically expressed in gigawatt-days per tonne (GWd/t)",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "fuel"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predominant method is the PUREX (plutonium-uranium reduction extraction) process, an aqueous hydrometallurgical technique developed in the 1940s and first commercially applied in the 1960s",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "technique"
    },
    {
      "text": "India employs a modified PUREX variant for its thorium-based cycle, recovering uranium and plutonium for fast breeder test reactors",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "india"
    },
    {
      "text": "These operations have recycled over 130,000 tons of spent fuel globally by 2024, demonstrating technical maturity, though China and others are scaling up for self-sufficiency",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "operations"
    },
    {
      "text": "Advanced variants like UREX+ aim to mitigate risks by co-extracting plutonium with neptunium , but deployment lags due to regulatory and economic hurdles",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "advanced"
    },
    {
      "text": "The primary classes include exempt waste (EW), very low-level waste (VLLW), low-level waste (LLW), intermediate-level waste (ILW), and high-level waste (HLW)",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "primary"
    },
    {
      "text": "EW consists of materials with activity concentrations below exemption levels, posing negligible radiological risk and often cleared for conventional disposal",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "levels"
    },
    {
      "text": "VLLW and LLW encompass short-lived, low-activity materials such as contaminated tools, clothing, and resins from reactor operations, requiring shallow land burial or engineered near-surface facilities",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "short"
    },
    {
      "text": "ILW includes resins, chemical sludges, and components with higher activity or longer-lived isotopes, necessitating intermediate-depth disposal with shielding",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "ilw"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cumulative global spent fuel generation reached approximately 400,000 tonnes of heavy metal (tHM) by 2022, with annual production around 10,000-12,000 tHM from operating reactors",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "generation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boiling water reactors (BWRs) feature similar core arrangements but allow boiling within the vessel, integrating steam separation directly",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "arrangements"
    },
    {
      "text": "These assemblies are supported by a core plate and shroud to maintain geometry under thermal and hydraulic stresses, ensuring efficient neutron flux distribution",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "assemblies"
    },
    {
      "text": "Structural materials like stainless steel and Inconel resist corrosion and irradiation-induced swelling, designed for 40-60 year lifespans with periodic inspections",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "like"
    },
    {
      "text": "Funding shortfalls or regulatory delays can extend timelines, but empirical data from over 100 completed U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "regulatory"
    },
    {
      "text": "Funding shortfalls or regulatory delays can extend timelines, but empirical data from over 100 completed U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "regulatory"
    },
    {
      "text": "Funding shortfalls or regulatory delays can extend timelines, but empirical data from over 100 completed U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "regulatory"
    },
    {
      "text": "Funding shortfalls or regulatory delays can extend timelines, but empirical data from over 100 completed U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "regulatory"
    },
    {
      "text": "Funding shortfalls or regulatory delays can extend timelines, but empirical data from over 100 completed U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "regulatory"
    },
    {
      "text": "These figures exclude overruns, which have historically inflated total costs by 100% or more in Western projects due to delays and changes",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "these"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conversely, Western projects frequently exceed 10\u201315 years; the U",
