    },
    {
      "text": "Surveys indicate that while overall U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "surveys"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mainstream outlets, influenced by environmental advocacy and aversion to centralized technologies, frequently amplify outlier risks while underreporting routine operations or comparative hazards from fossil fuels",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "outlets"
    },
    {
      "text": "This pattern underscores how selective emphasis sustains apprehension, even as operational data affirms nuclear's reliability",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "pattern"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-profile incidents like Chernobyl and Fukushima amplify perceptions of inherent danger, yet direct radiation casualties remain minimal relative to energy output and comparable events",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "high"
    },
    {
      "text": "Evacuation-related stress contributed to indirect deaths exceeding those from radiation , highlighting causal factors beyond the technology itself",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "evacuation"
    },
    {
      "text": "In reality, the volume of high-level waste from nuclear power is negligible: all spent fuel generated by U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "volume"
    },
    {
      "text": "In reality, the volume of high-level waste from nuclear power is negligible: all spent fuel generated by U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "volume"
    },
    {
      "text": "In reality, the volume of high-level waste from nuclear power is negligible: all spent fuel generated by U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "volume"
    },
    {
      "text": "In reality, the volume of high-level waste from nuclear power is negligible: all spent fuel generated by U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "volume"
    },
    {
      "text": "In reality, the volume of high-level waste from nuclear power is negligible: all spent fuel generated by U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "volume"
    },
    {
      "text": "Over 95% of nuclear waste is low- or very low-level, readily handled like industrial effluents",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "level"
    },
    {
      "text": "Concerns over economic unviability persist, with assertions that nuclear power's capital-intensive nature renders it costlier than renewables or gas",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "concerns"
    },
    {
      "text": "Existing nuclear facilities, with capacity factors exceeding 90%, deliver electricity at $30\u2013$60/MWh, competitive with gas combined-cycle ($48\u2013$109/MWh) and superior when factoring carbon externalities",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "factors"
    },
    {
      "text": "Regulatory delays and financing risks inflate upfront costs, yet countries like France demonstrate scalable, low-carbon baseload at effective rates below fossil alternatives over plant lifetimes",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "regulatory"
    },
    {
      "text": "International regimes have constrained proliferation despite widespread adoption, as civilian uranium enrichment for power does not inherently enable rapid weaponization without deliberate diversion",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nuclear_power",
      "agent": "regimes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Englert and Higgs received the 2013 Nobel Prize in Physics for this theoretical framework, recognizing its profound impact on understanding the fundamental structure of matter",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "higgs"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has no electric charge and does not participate in strong interactions, distinguishing it from other bosons like the W and Z particles",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "interactions"
    },
    {
      "text": "The fundamental role of the Higgs boson arises from its association with the Higgs field, a ubiquitous scalar field proposed to fill all of space-time",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "higgs"
    },
    {
      "text": "Independently, physicists Robert Brout and Fran\u00e7ois Englert introduced a mechanism involving spontaneous symmetry breaking that endows gauge bosons with mass while preserving key symmetries",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "independently"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shortly thereafter, Peter Higgs developed a related framework, explicitly predicting the existence of a scalar boson associated with this process",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "higgs"
    },
    {
      "text": "These seminal works collectively established the Brout-Englert-Higgs-Guralnik-Hagen-Kibble mechanism , which became integral to the electroweak theory of the Standard Model",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "collectively"
    },
    {
      "text": "The long-sought experimental verification arrived nearly five decades later at the Large Hadron Collider (LHC) at CERN",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "experimental"
    },
    {
      "text": "This field is invariant under local SU(2)<sub>L</sub> \u00d7 U(1)<sub>Y</sub> gauge transformations and interacts with other fields through specific terms in the Lagrangian",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "field"
    },
    {
      "text": "The VEV breaks the electroweak gauge symmetry spontaneously, setting the scale for particle masses in the theory",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "vev"
    },
    {
      "text": "These interactions underpin the acquisition of mass by fundamental particles via the Higgs field",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "these"
    },
    {
      "text": "The spontaneous breaking produces three would-be Goldstone bosons from the Higgs doublet's degrees of freedom, which are massless in the absence of gauge interactions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "spontaneous"
    },
    {
      "text": "This absorption ensures unitarity in high-energy scattering processes and maintains the theory's renormalizability",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "absorption"
    },
    {
      "text": "The historical development, building on Goldstone's theorem for global symmetries extended to local gauge theories, thus provided a consistent framework for electroweak unification",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "development"
    },
    {
      "text": "For the electroweak gauge bosons, the masses arise from the covariant derivative terms in the Lagrangian after the VEV substitution",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "electroweak"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Higgs mechanism ensures the electroweak theory remains perturbative at low energies by addressing issues of unitarity and renormalization",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "higgs"
    },
    {
      "text": "Similar constraints from CMS yield \u0393 H = 3",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "similar"
    },
    {
      "text": "These measurements leverage off-shell contributions, where the Higgs is produced slightly above its mass threshold, to probe the width without relying on production cross-sections alone",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "higgs"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ongoing Run 3 analyses have provided evidence for off-shell Higgs production and improved sensitivities to rare decays like H \u2192 \u03bc\u03bc",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "analyses"
    },
    {
      "text": "Complementary CMS results from similar channels yield consistent bounds, such as \u03ba \u03bb \\kappa_\\lambda \u03ba \u03bb \u200b between -2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "complementary"
    },
    {
      "text": "Complementary CMS results from similar channels yield consistent bounds, such as \u03ba \u03bb \\kappa_\\lambda \u03ba \u03bb \u200b between -2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "complementary"
    },
    {
      "text": "Complementary CMS results from similar channels yield consistent bounds, such as \u03ba \u03bb \\kappa_\\lambda \u03ba \u03bb \u200b between -2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "complementary"
    },
    {
      "text": "Complementary CMS results from similar channels yield consistent bounds, such as \u03ba \u03bb \\kappa_\\lambda \u03ba \u03bb \u200b between -2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "complementary"
    },
    {
      "text": "Complementary CMS results from similar channels yield consistent bounds, such as \u03ba \u03bb \\kappa_\\lambda \u03ba \u03bb \u200b between -2",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "complementary"
    },
    {
      "text": "Quartic coupling constraints remain weaker but are also compatible, derived indirectly from vector boson scattering processes observed in ATLAS and CMS data",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "quartic"
    },
    {
      "text": "These results highlight the Higgs boson's role in stabilizing the electroweak vacuum without evidence for beyond-Standard-Model modifications as of 2025",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "higgs"
    },
    {
      "text": "These advances leverage larger integrated luminosities and refined analysis techniques, strengthening tests of the Standard Model predictions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "advances"
    },
    {
      "text": "These decay modes are crucial for experimental detection at the LHC, where observability depends on the cleanliness of the signatures and background rejection",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "cleanliness"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bosonic decays like H \u2192 \u03b3\u03b3 and H \u2192 gg indirectly constrain these couplings through loop contributions dominated by the top quark Yukawa",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "contributions"
    },
    {
      "text": "Additionally, ATLAS reported evidence for H \u2192 \u03bc\u03bc decay in July 2025",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "additionally"
    },
    {
      "text": "These results underscored the LHC's superior energy reach while revealing the technical hurdles of managing enormous data volumes and multiboson backgrounds",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "results"
    },
    {
      "text": "These results marked the first time both experiments independently crossed the 5\u03c3 threshold conventionally required for a discovery in particle physics",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "results"
    },
    {
      "text": "This breakthrough validated decades of theoretical work and opened the door to precise measurements of the boson's properties",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "breakthrough"
    },
    {
      "text": "No significant deviations from SM expectations were observed in spin-parity tests, ruling out alternative hypotheses like spin-2 gravitons at high confidence",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "expectations"
    },
    {
      "text": "These fits assume SM-like production and decay, yielding signal strengths \u03bc \u2248 1",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "decay"
    },
    {
      "text": "These fits assume SM-like production and decay, yielding signal strengths \u03bc \u2248 1",
