    {
      "text": "This foundational result earned them the 1999 Nobel Prize in Physics and solidified the Higgs as a cornerstone of the theory",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "result"
    },
    {
      "text": "Alternative Theories In the Standard Model , the Higgs boson is an elementary scalar field responsible for electroweak symmetry breaking",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "higgs"
    },
    {
      "text": "This structure predicts deviations in Higgs couplings and branching ratios that can be tested experimentally",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "structure"
    },
    {
      "text": "These models predict new particles like KK gluons or radions (scalar fluctuations of the extra dimension metric) that influence Higgs production and decay",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "these"
    },
    {
      "text": "Overall, these constraints favor scenarios where new physics effects are suppressed near the electroweak scale, aligning the observed Higgs with Standard Model predictions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "effects"
    },
    {
      "text": "Searches for deviations in Higgs couplings offer windows into physics beyond the SM (BSM)",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "searches"
    },
    {
      "text": "This metastability arises from the shape of the Higgs potential at high field values, influenced by quantum corrections",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "metastability"
    },
    {
      "text": "This naming choice highlighted Higgs's 1964 paper, which explicitly predicted the associated scalar boson , though the mechanism itself was concurrently developed by multiple groups",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "this"
    },
    {
      "text": "In response, some physicists proposed more inclusive alternatives, such as the \"ABEGHHK'tH boson,\" an acronym honoring Philip W",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "physicists"
    },
    {
      "text": "In popular media, the Higgs boson earned the nickname \"God particle,\" originating from Leon M",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "higgs"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lederman's 1993 book The God Particle: If the Universe Is the Answer, What Is the Question",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "particle"
    },
    {
      "text": "Educational Analogies and Media Coverage To explain the Higgs mechanism to non-experts, physicists have employed several analogies",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Higgs_boson",
      "agent": "higgs"
    },
    {
