    {
      "text": "As a small and frail infant, his survival was uncertain, yet he outlived expectations amid a modest farming family of Puritan background",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Isaac_Newton",
      "agent": "yet"
    },
    {
      "text": "Priority Disputes with Contemporaries Newton's most prominent priority dispute arose with Robert Hooke concerning the inverse-square law of gravitational attraction",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Isaac_Newton",
      "agent": "hooke"
    },
    {
      "text": "Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia ruled in Marconi Wireless Telegraph Co",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Nikola_Tesla",
      "agent": "columbia"
    },
    {
      "text": "At its core lies the supermassive black hole Sagittarius A *, with a mass equivalent to about 4 million Suns",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Milky_Way",
      "agent": "core"
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1927, Jan Oort provided the first empirical evidence for the Milky Way's differential rotation by analyzing the proper motions of nearby stars",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Milky_Way",
      "agent": "oort"
    },
    {
      "text": "Darwin viewed slavery as a moral atrocity that degraded both enslavers and enslaved, contradicting claims of inherent racial inferiority used to justify it",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Charles_Darwin",
      "agent": "darwin"
    },
    {
      "text": "Secreted proteins are exported from the cell through the secretory pathway, functioning in extracellular environments like the bloodstream or tissue matrices",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Protein",
      "agent": "proteins"
    },
    {
      "text": "Additional brush-border enzymes, such as aminopeptidases and dipeptidases from enterocytes, complete the process by liberating free amino acids and di- or tripeptides",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Protein",
      "agent": "enzymes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elected a Fellow of the Royal Society in 1824, he received numerous honors, though he declined a knighthood and presidency of the Society",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Michael_Faraday",
      "agent": "society"
    },
    {
      "text": "Impressed by the young man's diligence and intellect, Davy appointed Faraday as his chemical assistant at the Royal Institution on March 1, 1813",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Michael_Faraday",
      "agent": "man"
    },
    {
      "text": "Faraday passed away on August 25, 1867, at age 75 in his Hampton Court residence",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Michael_Faraday",
      "agent": "faraday"
    },
    {
      "text": "Faraday's adherence to Sandemanianism involved periods of tension; he was excluded from the church in 1844 amid a congregational dispute but was reinstated",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Michael_Faraday",
      "agent": "faraday"
    },
    {
      "text": "In March 2025, NIST selected the HQC algorithm for standardization as part of the fourth round of the process",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Computer_science",
      "agent": "2025"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sagan rejected the label of atheist, describing it as requiring definitive knowledge of God's nonexistence, which he deemed unattainable given the limits of human evidence",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Carl_Sagan",
      "agent": "sagan"
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1997, NASA renamed the Mars Pathfinder lander the Carl Sagan Memorial Station to commemorate his advocacy for planetary exploration",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Carl_Sagan",
      "agent": "nasa"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elliptical galaxies appear smooth and featureless, lacking significant gas or dust, and range from nearly spherical to highly elongated shapes dominated by older, reddish stars",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Galaxy",
      "agent": "featureless"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rudolf II promptly appointed Kepler as Imperial Mathematician, a position that secured his role in continuing and refining Brahe's work",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Johannes_Kepler",
      "agent": "ii"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kepler interpreted this law not merely as a mathematical relation but as evidence of cosmic proportions ordained by God, blending empirical rigor with archetypal ideals",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Johannes_Kepler",
      "agent": "kepler"
    },
    {
      "text": "In 2024, the FDA cleared 221 AI devices, followed by 147 in the first five months of 2025, reflecting accelerated regulatory acceptance for diagnostic aids",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Artificial_intelligence",
      "agent": "fda"
    },
    {
      "text": "MD provides insights into phase transitions and transport properties, such as viscosity in polymer melts, with trajectories spanning femtoseconds to microseconds",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Thermodynamics",
      "agent": "md"
    },
    {
      "text": "Both organelles are bounded by double membranes, with the inner membrane derived from the symbiont's plasma membrane and the outer from the host's phagocytic vesicle",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cell_(biology)",
      "agent": "organelles"
    },
    {
      "text": "Trigonometric integrals often involve powers or products of sine, cosine, secant, or tangent",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Calculus",
      "agent": "trigonometric"
    },
    {
      "text": "Galileo's duties emphasized practical mathematics , including the design of instruments for measurement and fortification , aligning with Venetian interests in military engineering",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Galileo_Galilei",
      "agent": "s"
    },
    {
      "text": "Galileo regarded his Paduan years as the most fruitful of his life, marked by intellectual freedom under Venetian tolerance compared to stricter Tuscan oversight",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Galileo_Galilei",
      "agent": "galileo"
    },
