    {
      "text": "Bond dissociation energies (BDEs) quantify the enthalpy required to break a specific bond homolytically into radicals, contributing to the net energy change in reactions",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Chemistry",
      "agent": "enthalpy"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fringe claims, such as those in self-published works asserting verbatim copying, lack substantiation from primary documents and often stem from non-peer-reviewed outlets",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Albert_Einstein",
      "agent": "fringe"
    },
    {
      "text": "Phonons here represent quantized vibrations of the lattice, analogous to harmonic oscillator modes",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Quantum_mechanics",
      "agent": "phonons"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fermentation technology, a foundational bioprocess , harnesses microbial metabolism for metabolite production, as in penicillin synthesis using Penicillium fungi scaled industrially since the 1940s",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Biotechnology",
      "agent": "synthesis"
    },
    {
      "text": "Feynman's Lectures on Computation, delivered at Caltech in 1983 and 1984, were compiled and published posthumously in 1996 by Addison-Wesley , edited by Anthony J",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Richard_Feynman",
      "agent": "feynman"
    },
    {
