      "agent": "kennedy"
    },
    {
      "text": "Accompanying the speech, Kennedy transmitted a formal letter to Soviet Premier Nikita Khrushchev via diplomatic channels, reiterating the U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "kennedy"
    },
    {
      "text": "Over the ensuing days, the leaders exchanged additional public messages, with Khrushchev on October 26 sending a lengthy personal letter\u2014intercepted and read by U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "over"
    },
    {
      "text": "However, a second Khrushchev message issued publicly on October 27 adopted a harder line, conditioning missile removal on the additional U",
