      "agent": "s"
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite military advisors urging defiance or limited escalation, Khrushchev prioritized de-escalation, viewing the deployment as a defensive gamble that had overextended Soviet capabilities",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "despite"
