      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "authorities"
    },
    {
      "text": "Internally, the leadership experienced strain, with Castro reportedly falling ill from exhaustion amid the perceived abandonment by Moscow",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "leadership"
    },
    {
      "text": "This outcome fueled perceptions of Khrushchev's adventurism as reckless, exposing Soviet vulnerabilities in projecting power and deterring U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "outcome"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-ranking officials, including defense ministers and party elites, expressed private dissatisfaction with the crisis management, viewing it as a failure to match U",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "high"
    },
    {
      "text": "These internal tensions compounded existing grievances over Khrushchev's domestic reforms and agricultural policies, accelerating a leadership challenge",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "tensions"
    },
    {
      "text": "Domestically, the crisis enhanced Kennedy's political standing, offsetting prior criticism from the Bay of Pigs failure and demonstrating presidential resolve against Soviet adventurism",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "crisis"
    },
    {
      "text": "This support manifested in rhetorical and procedural backing for the quarantine, reinforcing executive discretion in foreign policy crises without formal declarations of war",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "support"
    },
    {
      "text": "These insights informed subsequent US doctrine, prioritizing flexible response over massive retaliation to sustain deterrence amid proliferating threats",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "insights"
    },
    {
      "text": "These measures, while limited, established precedents for future accords like the 1968 Non-Proliferation Treaty, underscoring the crisis's role in shifting from confrontation to cautious restraint",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Cuban_Missile_Crisis",
      "agent": "these"
    },
    {
      "text": "This unity contrasted with pre-crisis divisions over U",
