      "source": "Grokipedia-Adolescence",
      "agent": "criminal"
    },
    {
      "text": "For instance, an agent may intend to abstain from indulgence but succumb impulsively, revealing a disconnect between intention and agential efficacy",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Agency_(philosophy)",
      "agent": "impulsively"
    },
    {
      "text": "Experimental manipulations of free will beliefs reveal agency 's functional role in moral and prosocial behavior",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Agency_(philosophy)",
      "agent": "experimental"
    },
    {
      "text": "Skepticism about agency extends illusionism by questioning the foundational reality of human self-determination , often rooted in naturalistic critiques of the unified self",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Agency_(philosophy)",
      "agent": "illusionism"
    },
    {
      "text": "Such protocols address data indicating that 10-20% of requests involve treatable psychiatric factors, where autonomy claims may reflect distorted rationality rather than genuine self-determination",
      "source": "Grokipedia-Autonomy",
      "agent": "data"
    },
    {
      "text": "Successful nonviolent outcomes also correlate with lower relapse into authoritarianism , as broader involvement fosters resilient institutions compared to violent paths that empower narrow vanguards",
